# Cloudflare Pages headers for the docs host.
#
# The same policy `deploy/Caddyfile` applies when this site is served from the box,
# written in the format Pages reads. Keep the two in step: a docs page served from
# `docs.suite.run` should not have a different posture depending on whether it came
# from Caddy or from Pages.
#
# `script-src` needs `'unsafe-inline'` because Fumadocs hydrates React islands and
# writes the theme before the first paint. There is no user content on this origin,
# which is what makes the relaxation acceptable here and nowhere else.
# `connect-src` stays `'self'`: the search dialog fetches its static index from here.

/*
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'

# Astro hashes everything under `_astro`, so a year is safe. The HTML is the
# freshness question, and a stale page is how a shipped fix reads as a bug.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
